      "writtenOn": "2023-08-01T16:58:10Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Your proposed version doesn\u0027t seem to work :(\n\nBut the initial version does, let\u0027s say this is our test string: \"0,1,2,3\"\nSo first we skip until a coma:\n\",1,2,3\"\nwe erase first coma, such that we write 0 in that place. *p \u003d 0 actually erases a coma in the string. \n\nThen we pass our original string, which has it\u0027s first coma zero-ed:\n\"0\\01,2,3\"\nand something like this we pass to utl_str2int. This function converts the first character(\u00270\u0027) and moves to the second (\u0027\\0\u0027). If that character is \\0 - it returns converted value.\n\nI\u0027ve seen similar approach in other BTA event but there is a possibility that I am wrong with something and it can be done better :D But that\u0027s my understanding until now ; )",
